%%{init: {"sequence": {"wrap": true, "width": 170, "noteMargin": 8}}}%%
%% Order lifecycle, part 1: outbox relay -> Kafka -> payment consumer -> PSP.
%% Source of docs/diagrams/order-lifecycle.svg. Part 2 (expiry, settlement, dashboard) is order-settlement.mmd.
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  participant P as Postgres
  participant X as worker relay
  participant K as Kafka orders.v1
  participant Pay as payment consumer
  participant PSP as payment-mock
  participant R as Redis pub/sub
  participant G as api WS gateways

  Note over P,X: Woken by LISTEN outbox (checkout, cancel, expiry batches) or a 250 ms tick
  X->>P: BEGIN + pg_try_advisory_xact_lock(relay)
  X->>P: SELECT pending outbox rows, LIMIT 500, SKIP LOCKED
  X->>K: produce key=productId, acks=all, await delivery (message.timeout.ms 10 s)
  X->>P: mark published_at, COMMIT
  Note over X,K: Send failure → ROLLBACK and back off. Crash before COMMIT re-publishes the batch, consumers dedupe

  K->>Pay: order.placed
  Pay->>P: SELECT order
  alt already PAID
    Pay->>Pay: duplicate, no-op
  else EXPIRED, CANCELLED or PAYMENT_FAILED
    Pay->>PSP: close reference (refunds any charge)
  else PENDING_PAYMENT
    Pay->>PSP: POST /v1/charges, key charge:orderId
    Note right of PSP: timeout or 5xx: pause partition, retry same key, never DLQ
    alt succeeded
      PSP-->>Pay: succeeded
      Pay->>P: CAS to PAID + payments SUCCEEDED + outbox order.paid + inventory
      opt CAS lost to expiry or cancel
        Pay->>PSP: close reference (refund + fence)
        Pay->>P: payments row REFUNDED
      end
    else declined or reference_closed
      PSP-->>Pay: declined or reference_closed
      Pay->>P: CAS to PAYMENT_FAILED + payments FAILED + quota + outbox + inventory
    end
    Pay-)R: PUBLISH fd:ch:user:userId
    R-)G: fan-out to the buyer's sockets
  else any other status (RESERVED, REJECTED)
    Pay->>K: InvariantViolation → orders.v1.dlq + alert
  end

  K->>Pay: order.expired / order.cancelled
  Pay->>PSP: close reference, refunds a late charge
  Pay->>P: payments row REFUNDED if a charge was refunded
